      "id": 1,
      "text": "Lake Peekskill was once called Cranberry Pond because wild cranberries grew along its banks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://putnamvalleyhistory.org/historic-lake-peekskill/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the early 20th century, developer McGolrick bought the land and turned the small pond into the planned community of Lake Peekskill.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://putnamvalleyhistory.org/historic-lake-peekskill/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Hudson Valley Engineering Company mapped the area in 1929, and surveyor Chase signed the maps for the New York Title and Mortgage Company.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://putnamvalleyhistory.org/historic-lake-peekskill/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A free bus ran from the railroad station directly into Lake Peekskill, offering buyers a convenient tour of the developing property.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://putnamvalleyhistory.org/historic-lake-peekskill/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The community sits 3.7 miles northeast of the city of Peekskill, centered around the lake that gives the hamlet its name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Peekskill%2C_New_York",
